.git
.worktrees
domibus
nginx
docs/prompts
.schematron
log
tmp
vendor/bundle
.bundle
.env*
# `COPY . /usr/src/app` in the Dockerfile would otherwise put the credentials
# key into a layer of the image, where a secret has no reason to be: nothing
# the application reads is in its credentials, and production takes
# SECRET_KEY_BASE from the environment.
config/master.key
# Exceptions named one by one, and above all without a wildcard: a re-inclusion
# pattern containing `*` stops BuildKit pruning the excluded directories. It then
# walks the whole tree, `domibus/` included, whose contents it cannot read while
# the container is running — the build fails on
# "open domibus: permission denied".
!.env.template
!.env.oots.template
!.env.domibus.template
